Bug Report: ODT Parser Crash on Nested Tables
=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=
=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D=3D

Environment:
  AILANG Parse: v0.7.2
  AILANG Runtime: v0.10.1
  OS: macOS 14.3 (Apple M2)
  File: report_z=C3=BCrich_q1.odt (2.3 MB)

Steps to Reproduce:
  1. Create an ODT with a table containing a nested table in cell B2
  2. The inner table has merged cells spanning 3 columns
  3. Parse with: ailang run docparse/ report.odt blocks

Expected: Block ADT with nested Table blocks
Actual: Runtime panic =E2=80=94 "index out of range [3] with length 2"

Stack trace:
  odf_parser.ail:142 =E2=80=94 parseTableRow()
  odf_parser.ail:98  =E2=80=94 parseTable()
  odf_parser.ail:67  =E2=80=94 parseContent()
  format_router.ail:45 =E2=80=94 route()

The issue is that parseTableRow() uses the parent table's column =
count instead of the nested table's column count when allocating =
the cell array.

Workaround: Flatten nested tables before parsing (loses structure).

Proposed fix: Pass column count as parameter to parseTableRow() =
instead of reading from module-level state.

Priority: P1 =E2=80=94 blocks our Z=C3=BCrich office quarterly report pipeline.

Regards,
Fran=C3=A7ois M=C3=BCller
Senior Data Engineer, Z=C3=BCrich

